Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Yes, I can definitely help you with that!  To write an if/then statement in C, you basically want to write two parts together:

if statement with a condition you want to check
then part which contains code that will get executed if the condition is true

For example, if you wanted to make sure that a value is non-negative, you could write something like this:

if (value >= 0) {
    doSomething();
} else {
    doSomethingElse();
}
